<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpu Prapanca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1365">1365</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Prapanca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mpu Prapanca was a Buddhist court poet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a> poem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagarakretagama">Nagarakretagama</a> (Desawarnana), completed in 1365. Written in praise of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a>, the poem describes the royal capital, the king's progresses through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> and the lands claimed by Majapahit, and is a chief source for the kingdom at its height.</p></div>
